module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.occurrence_identity_compared_as_structure

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data occurrence_identity_compared_as_structure: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "occurrence_identity_compared_as_structure" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a control claiming equality of parsed structure compares whole Node values, or their byte renderings, including OccurrenceMinted allocator ordinals. The occurrence_identity_scope_law in std.occurrence_identity makes those ordinals unique only within one explicit allocator scope. What else that allocator minted changes the ordinals; equal ordinals from separate parses do not establish occurrence identity. A full parse and a heads parse mint different populations when one reads bodies and the other skips them. HARM: matching declaration structures compare unequal because the control asks an allocation question as part of its structural question. The same false negative affects any full-versus-partial parse comparison that includes minted ids, not only a census differential.",
    "EXECUTED SPECIMEN (2026-09-11, gunbc#11092, review 64052 cutover validation): cli_run::closure_edge_demand_tests::heads_and_resolved_readings_agree_on_candidate_and_variant_gating, fixture a.dag, declares module frontier, type Box<T> { value: T }, type Choice = First | Second, fn generic<T>(x: T) -> Box<T> { Box { value: x } }, and fn duplicated() -> Int { 1 }. With both normalizers using v1.compiler.compile::census_heads_module_node, an added full == heads assertion over census_heads_both_readings failed. Comparing its printed operands after removing ONLY OccurrenceMinted ordinal values made the remaining text identical. That diagnostic comparison established the specimen; it is not a proposed normalization implementation or an identity authority. A second run showed the same defect even for heads-versus-heads when production advanced the intern/occurrence snapshot before the differential read it. The shipped regression supplies the SAME incoming snapshot to both heads readers and compares the differential HEADS result with production HEADS, which catches the hand-strip/generated-strip fork without equating full and partial allocation histories. The existing full/heads differential policy and parse witnesses are unchanged.",
    "RUNG: outside the ladder for the class. Whole-Node equality remains writable and returns an ordinary Boolean with no refusal explaining the allocator-scope mismatch. The executed assertion is evidence of this specimen, not an acceptance-path wall preventing other consumers from choosing the wrong relation. No repository-wide protection is claimed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: a modeled structural-equality relation over Node that excludes minted occurrence ids, including nested declaration/signature subtrees, so structural consumers can ask that relation without manufacturing a second identity rule. Its availability would permit cutover of structural controls; it would not by itself make all misuse impossible. This receipt implements no such relation and changes no parse witness.",
    "NEIGHBOURS CHECKED: identity_absent_graph_traversal concerns the absence of an allowed visited key for synthesized nodes; here minted identity exists and is included in the wrong comparison. one_value_two_renderings_compared_for_equality concerns two spellings of one value; here the allocator values are actually different and need not be equal for the structural claim. comparison_keyed_on_part_of_the_identity_it_compares loses part of an identity and conflates distinct subjects; this class instead adds allocation identity to a structural comparison and falsely distinguishes matching structures.",
    "CLIMB, SEED-CHECKED .dag SOURCES ONLY (2026-10-25). For v2.std.node Node and Edge, the RUNG receipt above no longer holds on the seed-checker path (v1.compiler.infer). gunbc#14842 made Node and Edge equality-inadmissible, so a bare Node or Edge `==` refuses at acceptance and names its question: node_equal_ignoring_provenance (structure) or node_same_occurrence (occurrence). The derived-equality follow-up adds two things. A composite reaching Node compares member by member through a std.operator_realization EqualityPlan, which the checker computes once by declaration identity and the interpreter and emitter both execute. A bare Node member compares as a value (structure). A position that names one authored node is typed v2.std.node NodeOccurrence, whose == is node_same_occurrence, so which question a composite asks is fixed by the type of each position rather than by the caller's habit. STILL OUTSIDE: v1 host Rust (this row's executed specimen is cli_run Rust, which no .dag check reaches); the native v2 checker, which judges no == operand (gunbc.rung_drop native_equality_operand_judgment; v2 eval refuses a NodeOccurrence-reaching aggregate instead of answering); and generic positions instantiated to Node, which the walk admits instantiation-blind, plus collection membership on Node-reaching types; both are declared as gunbc.rung_drop derived_equality_residual_field_equality. The row's rung therefore stays unread at the class grain.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
